 steps='/'.join(f"{c['state_step_v']*1000:+.3f}" for c in cases);widths='/'.join('none' if c['pulse_width_us'] is None else f"{c['pulse_width_us']:.3f}" for c in cases)
 section=f'''\n## Autonomous local event-to-charge path - 2026-10-10\n\n[Boundary audit](../{rel(ap)}) and [catalog revision8](../{rel(cp)}):12 reusable module artifact sets and8 characterization assemblies. New native16MOS static control flip-flop passes zero/one/toggling capture and closed-slave hold. Native156MOS event sequencer includes four such control stages and interlocked clock phases. Three native-driver cases pass idle, one event with extra request while busy, and synchronous reset during event; no overlapping strobes. The earlier ideal-source run aborted at request fall1.8us; adding native input drivers completed with identical circuit/tolerances.\n\nThe physically joined230MOS4MIM sequencer/signed-injector assembly passes full DRC, physical flat LVS against frozen reference, independent GDS flat readback/LVS, LEF and1225-branch nonnegative extraction. Deep-hierarchy Netgen overflow and pre-repair sources are preserved. Three native50kHz request-to-charge runs give pulse widths{widths}us and state steps{steps}mV (small-positive/large-positive/large-negative). Each run uses one request and actual sequencer-generated SAMPLE/ARM/RECOVER/DONE; no externally prescribed WRITE/ARM timing. Two native MIM state loads initialize through reset TG; analog programming/bias/PARK references remain external.\n\nThis is local event sequencing only. Synchronous reset takes effect at capture; request while busy is not queued and upstream must obey valid/ready. Control bits do not replace analog membrane or weights. A five-cycle admission estimate gives50 events per5ms per engine at50kHz, not measured sustained throughput or full-population service. Bin/DAG completion, commit control, adaptation/inhibition/readout, references/programming, dense/full-chip layout and original-model accuracy remain incomplete. No goal completion claim.\n'''
 p=ROOT/'docs/RESULTS.md';s=p.read_text();i=s.index('\n## ');p.write_text(s[:i]+section+s[i:])
